{
  "id": 490,
  "description": "Welcome to The Den!\n================\nThis is the main branch of The Den, a semi-casual guild for my fellow lovers of progress bars and idle games. \n\nAre you lower level than combat 70? Check out our leveling guild, The Den Nest! \n\n\nRecruitment Requirements\n===================\n- Enjoy the game at your pace.\n- Contribute to the Challenges when you can, it helps the guild gain Marks which we need for Raids. \n- Please show some activity every week, whether it&#039;s a raid or item contribution to Challenges. \n- Minimum Total Level = 800, Combat Level = 70\n- We recommend a Combat Level of at least level 70, since that is what we raid regularly at the moment. If you are under level 70, check out our leveling guild, &quot;The Den Nest&quot;!\n- Join our Discord to stay connected with the guild. https://discord.gg/GA5hkVVN9F\n\nGuild Members\n===========\n- Communication - We have a discord created, https://discord.gg/GA5hkVVN9F\n\n- Raids - We run daily Raids at 6pm CST, please check the Guild page and/or Discord often for details. We&#039;ve been running double raids each night, make sure to switch locations!\n\n- Activity - I ask that everyone maintain weekly activity, whether it&#039;s a raid or an item contribution. The more our members are participating, the more XP we can all gain. I will kick members who have shown zero activity for a week. \n\n\nFAQ/Info\n=======\n- Challenges\n\nCompleting Challenges is a way for the Guild to earn Marks. These are just item exchanges. The items needed are randomly selected by the game. I or a guild Officer can generate a new round of Challenges every 24h. We earn 1 Mark per item challenge we complete. At our current guild level, we can generate 6 Challenges each round. \n\n- Marks \n\nMarks are the guild currency that we can earn by completing the Challenges here in the Guild tab. Marks are used to schedule Raids, and create Announcements for the guild. \n- Guild Level\n\nSelf-explanatory, this is just the level of our Guild. As far as I can tell, higher levels unlock more member slots, access to higher level Raids, and more Challenges at a time.\n- Guild Mastery\n\nThis is your own personal stat related to Guild participation. You earn XP here by contributing to Challenges, and joining Raids. \n- Raids\n\nThese are group battles that the entire Guild can join in on. As the guild levels up, we can clear higher level Raids. Each Raid is in a different map location, so keep an eye out on when/where Raids are happening. You will need to Travel to the zone in order to Join. Raids are a great way to earn some Gold, Combat XP, and Guild/Guild Mastery XP.",
